### Jet \(E_{{}_{T}}\) and Phi Resolution from PYTHIA Simulation

The \(E_{{}_{T}}\) resolution is not easy to determine to high precision. This is due to two opposing tendencies in jet-energy reconstruction. One tendency is that as \(E_{{}_{T}}\) increases, the absolute energy difference between true energy and reconstructed energy tends to increase proportionally. The other tendency is that as \(E_{{}_{T}}\) increases, more high-energy particles are produced. Higher energy particles are more collimated and less likely to be missed in jet reconstruction, lowering the difference between true and reconstructed jet energy.

